  "description": "Niddy: my personal .NET utilities. File-system extensions (retrying deletes, backups, copies, path matching), zip/tar archives, atomic file writes, debounced file watching, app paths, stream and string extensions, JSON files, humanized formatting, retry with backoff, Result and Option types, debounce/throttle and lock-free threading primitives, a rolling file logger, typed JSON settings stores, GitHub issue reporting, GitHub release update checks and verified downloads, file downloads (size limits, checksums, resuming) and reading text/JSON from the web, opening URLs, and platform-native secure storage (macOS Keychain, Windows Credential Manager, Linux Secret Service, with an encrypted-file fallback).",
